            <ArticleTitle>[Biocontrolled load tests].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is suggested to distinguish standard, conditionally standard and non-standard tests with loading. In conditionally standard tests the physiological functions are continuously analyzed during the examination, with the chosen criteria of threshold values being quantitative assay is made according to the value of the &quot;rousing&quot; loading effect. The techniques for the bicycle ergometry and passive orthostatic tests are elaborated in detail. The developed method yields comparable results, permits the automation of tests with loading and ensures the safety of examination.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
